{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-topological-mass-cat-descended","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:topological-mass-cat-descended","kind":"lemma","title":"Descended term equals the base-level mass","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-topological-mass-cat-eigenspace"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-topological-mass-cat-descended"],"tags":["descent","categorical-trace","ascent-embedding","mass"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_descended_is_base_mass","text":"topological-mass-cat-descended.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:topological-mass-cat-descended\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha = (\\int_A \\otimes \\mathrm{id}) \\circ \\Delta \\circ \\varrho</code>\nform the categorical mass integrand of a closed cycle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho</code> at level\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n+1</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho_0</code> denote its base-level <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-descent\">descent</a>. Then</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\bigl\\lVert \\mathrm{tr}(\\hat{\\tau}_n(\\alpha)) \\bigr\\rVert\n  =\n  \\mathfrak{m}(\\varrho_0).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-cat-descended.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"8.3.2"}
